{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/837043-it-came-from-beyond-the-umbra-a-50-s-wod","id":837043,"title":"IT Came from Beyond The Umbra!: a 50's WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-25T08:40:27-08:00","id":837043,"title":"IT Came from Beyond The Umbra!: a 50's WoD","content":"Im a huge fan of all the sci fi of the 50's and horror movies of that era. Things like The Thing, or The Blob.<br /> <br /> so i was thinking, How would you make the WoD as something set during the 50's sci fi era, to Dm a more Tongue and Cheek/Cheesy game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T09:13:25-08:00","id":837053,"title":"","content":"Atom-punk with a piece of Lovecraftian touch. My suggestion for an alien invader faction would be a mixture of biopunk version of (star treck) borgs and necromorphes.from &quot;dead space&quot; videogames. <br /> <br /> Also you can find like source of inspiration the movie &quot;invasion of body snatchers&quot; and the chimeres from &quot;Resistence: fall of man&quot;. <br /> <br /> But remember, the style of the canon WoD is &quot;monster are hidden among us but humanity doesn't notice&quot;. <br /> <br /> A crazy idea I have got for WoD are the &quot;nebulapolis&quot;, something like the mages' realm horizon, but they could be visited, explored and ruled by vampires, a mixture of the demiplane of dread from Ravenloft (D&amp;D setting) and the Metropolis from the rpg &quot;Kult: lost divinity&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T09:45:35-08:00","id":837059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/837043-it-came-from-beyond-the-umbra-a-50-s-wod#post837043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im a huge fan of all the sci fi of the 50's and horror movies of that era. Things like The Thing, or The Blob.<br /> <br /> so i was thinking, How would you make the WoD as something set during the 50's sci fi era, to Dm a more Tongue and Cheek/Cheesy game.</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually kinda did that. We called it Etherites: GO! It was an utterly pulpy and insane game about ancient tombs, giant monsters and alien invasions. The principals were all quite quirky (wo)men of Science, and the ST allowed us all one crazy over the top invention. Of the top of my head, there was an Aztec Hypertech Angel, a transformer, a village sized zeppelin, a molemachine, and a breeding project for the Creature from the Black Lagoon. Good times. Loads of fun.<br /> <br /> May i recommend trying out GURPS: Atomic Horror? It's an amazing resource for a game like this. There is also support for a campaign like this in the Revised Etherite book, but not as much as Atomic Horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T11:10:26-08:00","id":840033,"title":"","content":"I've run games in previous eras 'straight' and playing with pop-culture jokes, including <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> in both kitsch and gritty versions of the 70s, and a 1950s <b>Buffy The Vampire Slayer</b> game in the style of teens-versus-monsters B-movies. (I used <b>GURPS Atomic Horror</b> as a sourcebook for it as well.)<br /> <br /> Think about how far you want to push the joke. You could describe the monsters looking like 50s-style special effects - <b>The Thing From Another World</b> is pretty serious but the Thing itself still looks like an off-brand Frankenstein monster in a boiler suit. Equally, the Ray Harryhausen animated ships in <b>Earth Vs. The Flying Saucers</b> are fantastic.<br /> <br /> Similarly, how much of the 'normal' <b>World Of Darkness</b> do you want to include? Retro-ray-gun Etherites fighting Technocracy MIBs and robots as well as threats from beyond the Umbra would be enough for a game by itself, but would you also bring in vampires in smoky jazz clubs or Christopher Lee brooding in an old castle, or have the PCs face A Teenage Werewolf? (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell,_Book_and_Candle\" target=\"_blank\">Bell, Book And Candle</a>, a 1950 play and 1958 film about an underground community of witches, is a very early example of urban fantasy complete with beatnik nightclub.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:14:23-08:00","id":840270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/837043-it-came-from-beyond-the-umbra-a-50-s-wod?p=840033#post840033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've run games in previous eras 'straight' and playing with pop-culture jokes, including <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> in both kitsch and gritty versions of the 70s, and a 1950s <b>Buffy The Vampire Slayer</b> game in the style of teens-versus-monsters B-movies. (I used <b>GURPS Atomic Horror</b> as a sourcebook for it as well.)<br /> <br /> Think about how far you want to push the joke. You could describe the monsters looking like 50s-style special effects - <b>The Thing From Another World</b> is pretty serious but the Thing itself still looks like an off-brand Frankenstein monster in a boiler suit. Equally, the Ray Harryhausen animated ships in <b>Earth Vs. The Flying Saucers</b> are fantastic.<br /> <br /> Similarly, how much of the 'normal' <b>World Of Darkness</b> do you want to include? Retro-ray-gun Etherites fighting Technocracy MIBs and robots as well as threats from beyond the Umbra would be enough for a game by itself, but would you also bring in vampires in smoky jazz clubs or Christopher Lee brooding in an old castle, or have the PCs face A Teenage Werewolf? (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell,_Book_and_Candle\" target=\"_blank\">Bell, Book And Candle</a>, a 1950 play and 1958 film about an underground community of witches, is a very early example of urban fantasy complete with beatnik nightclub.)</div> </div> </div> </div>im thinking on a very over the top cheesy world of darkness..<br /> rayguns, robots that work with Klaatu Verada Niktu, giant ant people, Black Furies of the SS. a bit of the 50's sci fi mixed with some exploitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:16:33-08:00","id":840407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/837043-it-came-from-beyond-the-umbra-a-50-s-wod?p=840270#post840270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> im thinking on a very over the top cheesy world of darkness..<br /> rayguns, robots that work with Klaatu Verada Niktu, giant ant people, Black Furies of the SS. a bit of the 50's sci fi mixed with some exploitation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sounds like fun and as Asmodai said use the Sons of Ether, and all their tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:10:02-08:00","id":840874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/837043-it-came-from-beyond-the-umbra-a-50-s-wod?p=840407#post840407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Sounds like fun and as Asmodai said use the Sons of Ether, and all their tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>A 50s B-Movie WoD would probably be an alternate universe where the Sons of Ether took over the technocracy rather than being kicked out. Also, while it was more of a 70s thing, a conspiracy of supernatural housewives from different splats would be a great addition (I always it interesting that Samantha in Bewitched was married to an ad-man of all people, I mean, what better way to change the consensus than through a mortal lover who works in an industry with that much control over human perception and thought).'<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the cultural 50s is longer than the actual decade. It begins with the end of world war two and doesn't really end until Kennedy is assassinated, thus touching off the 60s unrest.<br /> <br /> Also, while it's not a WoD book, GURPS has a source-book on B-movies and the 50s in general that is absolutely wonderful and I would definitely recommend <i>GURPS Atomic Horror </i>as a guide to the attitudes and culture of the 50s from if nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 03-02-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T00:34:57-08:00","id":841171,"title":"","content":"So what did we learn? Everyone recommends GURPS: Atomic Horror!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T05:26:39-08:00","id":842492,"title":"","content":"I think both kinded and fomori could fit very well with Invasion of the Body Snatchers-style tales in that context, with Souleaters possibly amping it all to eleven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}